    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351-a1">

                <pb facs="1279" n="1255" xml:id="pg1255"/>

                <head>Annex 3</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">List of Articles of the Draft
                        Peace Treaty With Italy Which Are Still Unagreed</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 3—Frontier between Italy and Yugoslavia.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 4—Frontier between Italy and the Free Territory of
                    Trieste.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 10 bis—Austro-Italian Agreement of September 5, 1946.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 16, para. 2—Frontier between Yugoslavia and the Free
                    Territory of Trieste.</p>
                <list>
                    <item>Paras. 1, 3, 4, 5 of the US Proposal in the text of the Conference
                        Recommendation.</item>
                    <item>Para. 9—Powers of the Governor in cases not admitting of delay.</item>
                    <item>Para. 10<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>—Citizenship.</item>
                    <item>Para. 11—Free Port and Economic Questions: <list>
                            <item>Provisional Government.</item>
                            <item>Withdrawal of troops from the Free Territory.</item>
                            <item>Provisional Regime; Statute of the Free Territory of Trieste.
                                (Section 1 of the French Proposal—Resolution of the
                                Conference).</item>
                            <item>Clauses on the Free Port of Trieste.</item>
                        </list></item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 25A—Recognition of Albania as an Allied and Associated
                    Power.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 64, Part B, para. 1—Reparation for Albania, Ethiopia,
                    Greece and Yugoslavia.</p>
                <list>
                    <item>Paras. 2(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>), 6, 7 (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >a</hi>), (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>), (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >c</hi>) (Doc. CFM(46) (NY)17).<anchor n="93" xml:id="d351-f1"/></item>
                    <item>Part D—Reparation for other Powers (Doc. CFM(46) (NY)20).<anchor n="94"
                            xml:id="d351-f2"/></item>
                    <item>Part E—Compensation to Italian nationals for property removed for
                        Reparation purposes (Doc. CFM(46) (NY)17).</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 67—Claims on Germany (Doc. CFM(46) (NY)20, para. 5).</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 67, para. 4 (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>), (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>), (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>), (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">d</hi>)—Compensation for Damage to United Nations
                    property in Italy.</p>
                <list>
                    <item>Addition to para. 8(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>)—Definition of Ships
                        (Doc. CFM (NY)17, para. 3).</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 69—Italian Property in the territory of Allied and
                    Associated Powers.</p>
                <list>
                    <item>Para. 5 (<hi rendition="#italic">e</hi>), (<hi rendition="#italic">f</hi>)
                        of the Draft Treaty—Property in Ceded Territories.</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 71—General Economic Relations</p>
                <list>
                    <item>Para. 1—Time-limit for Art. 71.</item>
                    <item>1(<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) Private Enterprises; Civil
                        Aviation.</item>
                </list>
                <pb facs="1280" n="1256" xml:id="pg1256"/>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 72—Settlement of Disputes—in connection with Articles 65,
                    68 and Annexes 6, 7, and 8.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 74 bis—Non-participation of Italy in the International
                    Financial Commission in Greece.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 76—Settlement of Disputes concerning the interpretation
                    and execution of the Treaty.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Art. 77 bis—Non-participation in the benefits of the Treaty by
                    countries which have not ratified it.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Annex III—Economic and Financial Provisions relating to Ceded
                    Territories (referred to the Economic Experts).</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Annex VI—Part B. Insurance. (CFM(46) (NY)20, para. 6).</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Annex VII—Part I—Contracts. (CFM(46) (NY)20, para. 2).</p>
                <list>
                    <item>Part II—Periods of Prescription (CFM(46) (NY)20, para, 3).</item>
                    <item>Part IV—Miscellaneous (CFM(46) (NY)20, para. 4).</item>
                    <item>Part V—Special Provision relating to the USA.</item>
                </list>
                <p rendition="#flush">Annex IX—Free Territory of Trieste (Water and Electricity
                    Supplies).</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">Annex XIII—Property and Debts Provisions relating to the Free
                    Territory of Trieste.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d351-f1" n="93" xml:id="d351-f1-content">
                <p>Report of the Committee of Economic Experts to the Deputies on the Peace Treaties
                    with Italy and Rumania, November 16, 1946, circulated to the Council as document
                    CFM(46) (NY)17, November 18, 1946, <ref target="#pg1196">p. 1196</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d351-f2" n="94" xml:id="d351-f2-content">
                <p>Second Report of the Committee of Economic Experts, CFM(46) (NY)20, November 21,
                    1946, <ref target="#pg1227">p. 1227</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
